{"title":"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(Quick_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (Quick and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02a003520e3b830bd307b584d7777a3971b673fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{30-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"33\" /> also a positive integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb08f1c6cfc0feadf543b455cd706558e20a686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 5\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8062f128e803f5747ddd257f47e46fcdc1987b0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\le 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> or else <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/6/0a6e01d35d1df97577f5a87837e2b9d6c4de86ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-n$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> will be negative, resulting in a negative fraction.  We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/d/d7de921059a1c1a3c66ba2bddafb08c582fa335a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> or else the fraction's denominator will exceed its numerator making the fraction unable to equal a positive integer value.  Substituting all values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> gives us integer values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6a5dbdb9d29540236036605b4bed6d334be868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=15, 20, 24, 25, 27, 28, 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"210\" height=\"16\" />.  Counting them up, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6cecfe394f16d2d6d7bc6844d2d845b2a014f077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba0bc2f0333a00f7473fabd13308a2043124feeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac{n}{30-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"97\" height=\"36\" /> be a positive integer (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d42c8080f1f22bae152b5dc35922de7178496be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />). Rearranging gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/2564907958d843f16ddc4086270ee99195a1603f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = m(30 - n) \\implies mn - 30m + n = 0\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"18\" />\nTo factor using Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick, add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d2107bbfc3123135aeffb2aa80def1641d29a278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> to both sides:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/a/21a478215a07d1593d2d8e58efc77f26debf3819.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[mn - 30m + n - 30 = -30 \\implies (m + 1)(n - 30) = -30\\]\" width=\"445\" height=\"18\" />\nMultiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c404a12c18f988d1cf29ab7b598703f5b68d48f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(m + 1)(30 - n) = 30\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d42c8080f1f22bae152b5dc35922de7178496be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc904960ae0b6b8ddbf068fe3a7a102f945db2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + 1 \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/073a316ac579cfd25c71f523a8197347138b8376.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> can be any positive divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> except <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e70164f9217bff3da7e247d5d1c397d327bf18d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^1 \\cdot 3^1 \\cdot 5^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />, which has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594b44d689b193babc0227058df0d2f616c7a127.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 + 1)(1 + 1)(1 + 1) = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"20\" /> positive divisors. Excluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/72095ccd974fe09f86ee9490d69fe138c0e5fd38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + 1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> (which corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6fc266463b33c8b1c079a50909f3fd03ed5ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, violating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d1431ad346632b25a0e7b3f12ebe19723b3960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />) leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f73aa3e6a633c01e525461be0135218511ebb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 - 1 = \\mathbf{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> valid solutions, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6cecfe394f16d2d6d7bc6844d2d845b2a014f077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa010bcd6f123f47eb5120b9b95ecb5060bc114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{30-n} = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"97\" height=\"36\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f8b136ddd69fa7bbaf637eef38def08ee25a10a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6b5fe4e51ce2e84815996b23779135d630045e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\frac{30m}{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"84\" height=\"39\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4bea4f5ee837b0249288558f2fb73a871b264491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d0d6084da35ea953b63d4d2b02e1807fe90c569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+1\\mid 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />. Our answer is the number of proper divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/9767bf8f66fb41484b140a6b7969b4018744fc5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^1 3^1 5^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/064f4b3960407065bcea36a82982c9d759f44bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+1)(1+1)(1+1)-1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"276\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First of all, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/4/3e46957959c3cc8b10752402d0c1d472279f0b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\leq{29}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> because the denominator will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/8957184d2467856309fc7c862ce867a75f38e971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> and the fraction will be negative if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f6c2120958ba96ae3810a1f2b14ccbe1288e6a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e55fa1a6aa34297ad767654865bbbfc9e159ea68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[30-n\\geq{1}\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14dadfa75033956f70fcd7fee599432dda5e198a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n}{30-n} = \\frac{n-30+30}{30-n} = \\frac{n-30}{30-n}+\\frac{30}{30-n} = \\frac{30}{30-n}-1\\]\" width=\"440\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/6/0a6e01d35d1df97577f5a87837e2b9d6c4de86ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-n$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> must be a positive divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/0/de0c6587729ce4d537b0b7c096a976a28e846483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30=2\\times 3\\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> positive divisors. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd01de82c610a4db199b91b254e717b9a71207c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-n=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" /> is not obtainable because this will make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The seven other divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1565d37641f7a1712aeb69c36df301ccb12fd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,3,5,6,10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, can all be assigned to the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/6/0a6e01d35d1df97577f5a87837e2b9d6c4de86ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-n$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>The answer to the problem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6cecfe394f16d2d6d7bc6844d2d845b2a014f077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~G2JFForever\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dc833924673f125d27786a040940ba1a8476ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-n\\mid n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />. Then, by divisibility rules:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca4ce5470da503ce1b73b8719be1547baaa1c81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[30-n\\mid n+30-n\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7eae48c9d300fec333ab2fd9647c5bff299328d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[30-n\\mid 30\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/7662b6cac60e63f51bb4b02027f796442c1e8ac1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\mid 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"20\" /> isn't counted, meaning we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6cecfe394f16d2d6d7bc6844d2d845b2a014f077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We recognize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08c9bef70a567cc9c8f712228e25ae6f56048d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15\\le n &lt; 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> because for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02a003520e3b830bd307b584d7777a3971b673fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{30-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"33\" /> to be a positive integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/9394580abe33a6e157b74d9f1e430908c4b73e7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-n \\le n \\implies 2n \\ge 30 \\implies n \\ge 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"303\" height=\"16\" />. Testing the numbers in this range gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/795e1576020e56b13661b976d4ca5391b5ed77aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\{15, 20, 24, 25, 27, 28, 29\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"20\" />, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6cecfe394f16d2d6d7bc6844d2d845b2a014f077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~MathCosine\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28Quick_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(Quick_and_Easy)\">Video Solution 1 (Quick and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (Quick and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rN76FKYRjls\">https://youtu.be/rN76FKYRjls</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B\">2014 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <